        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Japan Airlines Co., Ltd. (JAL), J-Air Co., Ltd., All Nippon Airways\n- Places: Japan, Nagoya Airfield, Toyoyama, Nishikasugai District, Aichi\n- Topics: airline industry, flag carriers, regional commuter airlines\n\nFacts:\n- Japan Airlines Co., Ltd. (JAL) was incorporated in 1962.\n- Japan Airlines Co., Ltd. (JAL) is the flag carrier airline of Japan.\n- Japan Airlines Co., Ltd. (JAL) is the second largest airline in Japan behind All Nippon Airways.\n- J-Air Co., Ltd. is a regional commuter airline in the JAL group.\n- J-Air Co., Ltd. has its headquarters in the Terminal Building at Nagoya Airfield in Toyoyama, Nishikasugai District, Aichi, Japan.\n- J-Air Co., Ltd. has its main hub at Nagoya Airfield.",
